From 13eb71bd581291a76ca03950a96adcdaa47e1f9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Fiddaman <illumos@fiddaman.net>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:00:25 +0000
Subject: Revert "Silently ignore -pthread etc. on Solaris"

This reverts commit 832de2f102f for illumos.

The illumos <errno.h> only maps errno to the per-thread (*(___errno()))
when _REENTRANT or _TS_ERRNO is defined, or when _POSIX_C_SOURCE selects
POSIX.1c or later. Software that relies on -pthread for this would
otherwise bind to the process-global errno with no diagnostic. Other
headers such as <stdio.h> and <netdb.h> still test _REENTRANT too.
Keep defining _REENTRANT and _PTHREADS for -pthread and -pthreads until
illumos changes.
---
 gcc/config/i386/sol2.h |  4 ++++
 gcc/config/sol2.h      |  4 ++++
 gcc/config/sol2.opt    |  4 ++--
 gcc/doc/invoke.texi    | 13 ++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

